{
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 29/10/2025, the proposal as shown on the drawing(s) submitted on 29/10/2025 and numbered Unnumbered Supporting Planning Statement, Unnumbered Site Location Plan, A2 1, A2 2, A2 3, A2 4, A2 5, A0 6, 01 1.0, 02, 1.0, 01 2.0, 01 2.0 was not lawful within the meanings of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 because: \r\nThe proposed development fails to comply with the terms of Class A, Clauses A.1 (i) and A.3 (b) of Part 1 of Schedule 2 of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended). The proposed single storey rear extension and two storey rear extension is considered to be two elements comprising a single enlargement as one part of the enlargement could not be constructed without the other. Therefore, the proposed two storey element would be within 2 metres of the boundary of the curtilage of the dwellinghouse and would have an eaves height that exceeds 3 metres. The first floor side window would not be obscured glazed and non-opening above more than 1.7 metres above finished floor level. \r\nThe proposed development also fails to comply with the terms of Class B Clauses B.2 (b)(ii) and (c) of Part 1 of Schedule 2 of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended) as the proposed roof extension attaches to the two storey rear extension resulting in the enlargement beyond an outside face of the exterior wall of the original dwellinghouse. The proposed side windows on the side roof slope would not be obscure glazed and non-opening above more than 1.7 metres above finished floor level.\r\n"
  ],
